Hooks: every *.sh file here, and in ~/.config/regolith3/multisession/hooks.d/,
is sourced (bash) by 'regolith-multisession launch' just before a session
starts, in both modes. A failing hook is logged and ignored.

Available to hooks:
  MULTISESSION_SESSION   the session, e.g. regolith-x11
  MULTISESSION_MODE      primary (stock session) or standalone
  MULTISESSION_INSTANCE  1 for the user's first graphical session, 2, 3, ...
  MULTISESSION_RUNDIR    per-session runtime directory
  DISPLAY, XDG_VTNR, XDG_SESSION_ID, ...

Example, 50-instance-look.sh: a different Regolith look in later sessions
(regolith-session-x11 merges, so these win unless your Xresources set them):

  if [ "$MULTISESSION_MODE" = standalone ] && [ -f ~/.config/regolith3/Xresources-instance ]; then
      xrdb -merge ~/.config/regolith3/Xresources-instance
  fi
